d type(s) for *: 'NoneType' and 'int'\n```\n\nTrack down why this happens and fix it so the program runs cleanly. When it\nworks, `python3 main.py` should print exactly:\n\n```\nTotal: 5.0\n```\n\nDone when `python3 main.py` exits successfully and prints that line.\n"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 1, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "stdout", "first_after_build": false, "first_side": "without", "fresh_subagents": 1, "harness": "opencode", "harness_version": "0.0.0--202610170355 (/workspace/openbench-ab/results/opencode-src/bin/64e2bf8bf00eca1c6ad4486e29eb84f7907d1d35/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: task]\n[tool: task]\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nThe script runs now. `python3 main.py` prints `Total: 5.0` and exits with code 0.\n\n**Where `rate` becomes None:** at `app/pricing.py:8`, which runs `SETTINGS.get(\"rate\")`. `.get()` returns `None` when the key isn't there instead of raising an error. `app/report.py:9` then tries `None * 10`, which is the crash in your traceback.\n\n**Missing settings key:** I asked the same subagent again using the id from the first call. It confirmed that `settings.json` has no `\"rate\"` key. Line 2 has `\"rat\": 0.5` instead, which is a typo.\n\n**Fix:** I renamed `\"rat\"` to `\"rate\"` in `settings.json:2`.\n\nYou could also change `get_rate()` to use `SETTINGS[\"rate\"]`. Then a missing key would fail right away with a clear `KeyError` instead of a confusing `TypeError` later. I didn't make that change.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": ["